 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "PersistentKVStore() starts empty. set(key, value) stores or overwrites; get(key) returns the value or \"\" when absent; delete(key) returns whether a key was removed. save() returns the blob of the current state. The blob is a list of byte values 0..255: a 4-byte big-endian entry count, then for each entry in ascending key order a 4-byte big-endian key length, the key's ASCII bytes, a 4-byte big-endian value length and the value's ASCII bytes. load(blob) replaces the whole state with the entries of a well-formed blob (level 1 only receives blobs in this format). The Medium is modelled by the caller holding the blob. Every method call is answered in call order on one instance; void methods return nothing.",
  "provenance": [
   {
    "repository": "gamma",
    "revision": null,
    "path": "projects/algorithm_solver/catalogue/authored/hack2hire-chunk10-a-20261028-v1/contracts.json",
    "sha256": "be5d798382a43847401e76609d79932746e664be0d91c81b132bf6b46cd69126",
    "selector": "/problems/19/inferred_spec"
   }
  ]
 },
